# oracle.manifest — pinned third-party reference artifacts, BINARY ONLY.
#
# Format:  <kind> <name> <version> <sha256|-> <url|->
#   container  a container image, pulled by tag
#   file       a downloaded artifact, checksum-verified
#
# RULES
#   - Binaries and containers only. A source archive or a source repository
#     URL is REFUSED by tools/fetch_oracle.sh before it is fetched.
#   - Everything is pinned. An unpinned oracle is a moving target, and a
#     compatibility result that cannot name the version it was obtained
#     against is not a result.
#   - Nothing here is committed. The fetched content lands in oracle/, which
#     is gitignored: using a program creates no derivative work, but vendoring
#     its code would put GPL files in our history.
#
# Versions are left unset until the first real run pins them against a
# measured checksum. Guessing a version and a hash would produce a manifest
# that looks authoritative and verifies nothing.
#
# container  meshtastic/meshtasticd   <version>   -   -
# file       firmware-heltec-v3.bin   <version>   <sha256>   <release-asset-url>
